* OpenSSH\ncertificates
** Structure
*** user or host type
*** serial and key_id
*** principals, max 256
*** valid_after / valid_before
*** two option bags
*** signing CA key
*** no ASN.1, no chain
** Validation
*** type must match the use
*** half-open validity window
*** empty principal list\nrejected
*** wildcard set by caller
*** operator-readable reasons
** Critical options
*** restrict the holder
*** force-command
*** source-address
*** verify-required
*** unknown means reject
** Extensions
*** grant a privilege
*** permit-pty, permit-agent,\npermit-port-forwarding
*** no-touch-required
*** unknown means ignore
** Revocation
*** KRL sections
*** by serial, key id,\nkey blob, fingerprint
*** list / range / bitmap
*** cost model in bits
*** list may be signed
@endmindmap
